                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "13d8e294-b6d5-4f34-864d-48520492690b",
                        "source_entry_id": "d457c257-6e57-3563-bf90-57d209340115",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fcb30c6-7aa3-3a34-8ef0-f1a479affb5a",
                        "target_lang_word": "psychotherapist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "psychotherapist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8d4f911-48ec-3e9f-8d48-1e3b556807ba",
                                        "entry_id": "bfe17a54-8b39-3b0b-a03e-5c442d5b1919",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who practices psychotherapy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "532a1af9-0d38-4cec-a240-6046b7d3e33a",
                                                "sense_id": "e8d4f911-48ec-3e9f-8d48-1e3b556807ba",
                                                "text": "“Psychotherapists are not immune to the same stereotypes that we all have, and I think they could become even more relevant for psychotherapists than for other professions [both medical and nonmedical], because they are embarking on this intimate, potentially long-term relationship with these [clients],” said Heather Kugelmass, a doctoral student in sociology at Princeton University. Kugelmass is the author of the study (PDF), which was published Wednesday in the Journal of Health and Social Behavior."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4feceaaf-d326-4439-9e3b-06d9ca45be6f",
                                                "sense_id": "e8d4f911-48ec-3e9f-8d48-1e3b556807ba",
                                                "text": "A psychotherapist I visited a few years ago [...] told me that my mother leaving my father, and my father letting us both go, has coloured my view of all relationships."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89657e06-dce7-4c52-b080-c1f81907b1cd",
                                                "sense_id": "e8d4f911-48ec-3e9f-8d48-1e3b556807ba",
                                                "text": "“People don’t come to therapy until they’re having the equivalent of an emotional heart attack,” psychotherapist Lori Gottlieb told CNN Chief Medical Correspondent Dr. Sanjay Gupta on his podcast Chasing Life recently."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c3bcbd93-4946-41f0-9511-6786d6269b43",
                        "source_entry_id": "d457c257-6e57-3563-bf90-57d209340115",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fcb30c6-7aa3-3a34-8ef0-f1a479affb5a",
                        "target_lang_word": "psychoterapeut",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "341df519-47ff-4698-90fa-08866c7daa2e",
                        "source_entry_id": "d457c257-6e57-3563-bf90-57d209340115",
                        "source_sense_id": "6fcb30c6-7aa3-3a34-8ef0-f1a479affb5a",
                        "target_lang_word": "psychothérapeute",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "psychothérapeute",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6552f8ed-5634-352b-a016-e0f198028ee5",
                                        "entry_id": "3e077035-1515-3583-871f-c157138aa047",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Médecin ou personne (non diplômée de la faculté de médecine) spécialisé dans la thérapeutique du psychique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bcb5a61-b504-4eb1-a9b3-9be57cf0e056",
                                                "sense_id": "6552f8ed-5634-352b-a016-e0f198028ee5",
                                                "text": "Je n’avais pas voulu prendre ces lettres de menaces au sérieux… Pas au sérieux, non plus, les conseils de quelques amis médecins qui m’avaient suggéré de faire suivre Julie par un psychothérapeute…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02c4c295-6055-45eb-a73a-410e812200e6",
                                                "sense_id": "6552f8ed-5634-352b-a016-e0f198028ee5",
                                                "text": "Lucile était suivie par un psychiatre qui lui prescrivait les médicaments et un psychothérapeute qu’elle voyait deux fois par semaine, avec lequel elle avait entrepris un travail au long cours, dont les séances se heurtaient à son mutisme. Lucile n’avait rien à dire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "298dc93c-8556-4a71-80a1-6c54e63b4061",
                                                "sense_id": "6552f8ed-5634-352b-a016-e0f198028ee5",
                                                "text": "Selon le psychothérapeute Thomas d’Ansembourg, qui la décrit dans son best-seller Cessez d’être gentil, soyez vrai (Éditions de l’Homme), « Le non-respect de soi mène tôt ou tard au non-respect de l’autre »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
